\description{
\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

Builds a white-matter atlas from a volumetric label map. This is
\code{\link[=create_subcortical_from_volume]{create_subcortical_from_volume()}} under another name: a white-matter
atlas stores what a subcortical one stores -- polygons for the slab views
and a mesh per structure -- and is built the same way. Only the type of
the finished atlas differs, which is what lets a plot label it as white
matter while every method written for a subcortical atlas still applies.

Use this for a parcellation of white-matter \emph{regions}. White-matter
\emph{tracts} reconstructed as bundles are a different shape and belong in
\code{\link[=create_tract_from_volume]{create_tract_from_volume()}}, which also carries centerlines.
}
